  "notes": "A civic collections tool for proposing 12 works for a library exhibition. Warm off-white page (#f4f3ef) with white panels and a dark navy top bar. A deep teal / green / amber traffic-light system carries eligibility: RR/EA/CA space chips are green when eligible, amber with warnings and grey struck-through when not eligible. Condition dates go amber when stale. Proposal slots have colored left rails (green = ok, amber = warning, dashed = open). Constraint checking is explicit ('4 of 6 required (2 more)', wall-length meters 503/640). Native selects and checkboxes are used without custom styling. A shortlist star sits in each row; 'Propose' turns into a 'Slot N' pill once placed. The row detail opens in a right-side drawer with a scrim (verified live, not in the capture) showing a per-space fit calculation. The candidate list loads 150 rows at a time via 'Show 150 more'. Filter placement (inline toolbar selects) was filed as a new value."
